<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Two vectors with a given sum</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>\(\mathbf{c} = {@col(cv)@}\). Give two vectors \(\mathbf{p}\) and \(\mathbf{q}\) with \(\mathbf{p} + \mathbf{q} = \mathbf{c}\). Neither \(\mathbf{p}\) nor \(\mathbf{q}\) may be horizontal or vertical: each must have two non-zero components. (There are many correct answers.)</p><div>\(\mathbf{p} =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] \(\quad \mathbf{q} =\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]]</div><div>[[feedback:prt1]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Split each component of \(\mathbf{c}\) into two non-zero parts. For example, take \(\mathbf{q} = {@q1t@}\); then \(\mathbf{p} = \mathbf{c} - \mathbf{q} = {@p1t@}\). Check: \({@p1t@} + {@q1t@} = {@col(cv)@}\).</p><p>Drawn head to tail, \(\mathbf{p}\) then \(\mathbf{q}\) ends where \(\mathbf{c}\) ends.</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[validate_numeric(ex) := block([sx], sx: ev(ex, simp), if listofvars(ex) = [] and freeof(%i, sx) then "" else "Type a number in each box, not a letter.");
col(v) := matrix([v[1]],[v[2]]);
/* Design: give two vectors with a given sum, graded by property: any p and q with p + q = c and no zero component scores. Source: original. */
c1: rand_with_prohib(-8,8,[-1,0,1]); c2: rand_with_prohib(-8,8,[-1,0,1]);
cv: [c1,c2];
p1t: col([c1-1,c2-1]); q1t: matrix([1],[1]);
p2t: col([c1+1,c2+1]);
hv1: col([c1,0]); hv2: col([0,c2]);
bad1: col([c1+2,c2]); badm: matrix([q],[1]);
/* decimal test inputs (fairness) */
dp: float(col([c1/4,c2/4])); dq: float(col([3*c1/4,3*c2/4])); fh1: float(hv1); fh2: float(hv2);
]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
  <specificfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[]]></text></specificfeedback>
  <questionnote format="moodle_auto_format">
